       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it, and the decision is yours. But a scheduled 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine is a dose I can't identify any therapeutic use for. In an adult with normal kidney and liver function, it risks profound hypotension and shock, and the effects could last for days. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose:** for example, 10 mg by mouth once daily, which is the maximum. I can add a note if you plan to titrate.\n- **Enter a different regimen:** if the goal is stronger blood pressure control, I can enter a second agent at a standard dose.\n- **Route it through pharmacy:** if you have a rationale I'm not aware of, you can enter the order directly through your institution's high-dose override process. That process includes pharmacist verification.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
